<!-- LATEST ARTICLES SECTION -->
<section class="py-5 bg-black section" id="blog">
    <div class="container py-5">
        <SectionHeading Title="Latest Insights" Subtitle="Our Blog" />

        <div class="row g-4">
            @if (recentPosts == null)
            {
                <div class="col-12 text-center text-secondary">
                    <p>Loading recent articles...</p>
                </div>
            }
            else if (!recentPosts.Any())
            {
                <div class="col-12 text-center text-secondary">
                    <p>No articles found. Check back soon for updates!</p>
                </div>
            }
            else
            {
                @foreach (var post in recentPosts)
                {
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <ArticleCard
                            Image="@(post.FeaturedImage ?? "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1460925895917-afdab827c52f?w=800&q=80")"
                            Author="@post.Author" Category="@(post.Category?.Name ?? "Web Design")"
                            Date="@(post.PublishedAt?.ToString("MMMM dd, yyyy") ?? post.CreatedAt.ToString("MMMM dd, yyyy"))"
                            Title="@post.Title" Excerpt="@post.Summary" Link="@($"/blog/{post.Slug}")" />
                    </div>
                }
            }
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ SECTION -->
<section class="py-5 bg-dark section" id="faq">
    <div class="container py-5">
        <SectionHeading Title="Frequently Asked Questions" Subtitle="FAQ" />

        <p class="text-secondary text-center mx-auto mb-5" style="max-width: 760px;">Clear answers about how we build, support, advise and secure your technology.</p>
        <div class="accordion accordion-flush mx-auto" id="faqAccordion" style="max-width: 980px;">
            <FaqItem Category="Software Development" Icon="bi-code-square" Question="What kinds of software do you develop?">
                <Answer>
                    <p>We design and build secure web applications, business portals, APIs, mobile-ready systems and workflow automation. We begin with discovery, then provide a written scope, architecture approach, delivery milestones and acceptance criteria before implementation.</p>
                </Answer>
            </FaqItem>

            <FaqItem Category="Software Development" Icon="bi-calendar-check" Question="How long will a software project take?">
                <Answer>
                    <p>Timing depends on scope, integrations, data migration and assurance needs. After discovery, we divide delivery into clear milestones and provide a realistic schedule. Smaller systems may take weeks; larger platforms are normally delivered in phases.</p>
                </Answer>
            </FaqItem>

            <FaqItem Category="Database Services" Icon="bi-database-check" Question="Can you migrate or optimise an existing database?">
                <Answer>
                    <p>Yes. We can assess schema design, query performance, indexing, backup strategy, access controls and migration risk. Production changes are planned with validation, rollback and recovery requirements appropriate to the system.</p>
                </Answer>
            </FaqItem>

            <FaqItem Category="IT Support" Icon="bi-headset" Question="What does your IT support service cover?">
                <Answer>
                    <p>Coverage can include user support, endpoint and operating-system troubleshooting, account issues, networking, routine maintenance and incident coordination. Response targets and service hours are agreed in the support plan.</p>
                </Answer>
            </FaqItem>

            <FaqItem Category="Consultancy" Icon="bi-lightbulb" Question="When should we engage an IT consultant?">
                <Answer>
                    <p>Consultancy is useful before a major purchase, migration, system replacement or transformation programme—or when technology costs and risks are unclear. We assess the current state, identify options and provide an independent, prioritised roadmap.</p>
                </Answer>
            </FaqItem>

            <FaqItem Category="Penetration Testing" Icon="bi-shield-lock" Question="How does a penetration test work?">
                <Answer>
                    <p>Testing begins only after written authorisation and a defined scope. We agree targets, exclusions, testing windows and escalation contacts, then assess the authorised environment and deliver an evidence-based report with risk ratings and remediation guidance.</p>
                </Answer>
            </FaqItem>

            <FaqItem Category="Penetration Testing" Icon="bi-arrow-repeat" Question="Do you verify security fixes after testing?">
                <Answer>
                    <p>Yes. Retesting can be included in the engagement. We verify whether agreed findings were properly resolved and issue an updated status; we do not describe a system as completely secure because security risk changes over time.</p>
                </Answer>
            </FaqItem>

            <FaqItem Category="Engagement & Pricing" Icon="bi-clipboard-check" Question="How do pricing and project commencement work?">
                <Answer>
                    <p>We price against confirmed scope, complexity, risk and service levels. After an initial discussion, you receive written deliverables, assumptions, responsibilities, timeline and commercial terms. Work starts after approval and any agreed onboarding requirements are complete.</p>
                </Answer>
            </FaqItem>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

